1hg|v|To act upon; to produce an effect or change upon. ; To influence or move, as the feelings or passions; to touch. ; To love; to regard with affection. ; To show a fondness for; to like to use or practice; to choose; hence, to frequent habitually. ; To dispose or incline. ; To aim at; to aspire; to covet. ; To tend to by affinity or disposition. ; To make a show of; to put on a pretense of; to feign; to assume; as, to affect ignorance. ; To assign; to appoint.	o:1bhd,70,24;138,30,5;3tv,23,7;wbc,17,3;1kjz,12,5;c3g,7,3;1n1i,3,10;1n1q,2,5~1bhd,70,24;1n1i,3,10;3tv,23,7;138,30,5;1n1q,2,5;1kjz,12,5;c3g,7,3;wbc,17,3	s:1vkc,20,7~1vkc,20,7	d:1cd,92,3;1dbn,87,19;208h,48,8;1wdi,38,3;ivr,35,6;bwd,25,4;2ex,10,15~1dbn,87,19;2ex,10,15;208h,48,8;ivr,35,6;bwd,25,4;1wdi,38,3;1cd,92,3
